@node Options
@section Options

All options are in the customization group @code{code-review}, with its
subgroups @code{code-review-github} and @code{code-review-gitlab}.

@vtable @code
@item code-review-auth-login-marker
The symbol after @samp{^} in the login of your auth source entries.  The
default is @code{code-review}; set it to @code{forge} to use Forge's
tokens.

@item code-review-fill-column
The column at which comments are wrapped; default 80.

@item code-review-new-buffer-window-strategy
The function that shows a new review buffer; default
@code{switch-to-buffer-other-window}.

@item code-review-buffer-name
@itemx code-review-commit-buffer-name
@itemx code-review-comment-buffer-name
The names of the review, commit and comment buffers.

@item code-review-section-indent-width
The indentation of nested sections; default 1.

@item code-review-section-image-scaling
The scaling of images shown in the buffer; default 0.8.

@item code-review-lgtm-message
The message of @kbd{r l}; default @samp{LGTM! :thumbsup:}.

@item code-review-always-restrict-approval?
If non-@code{nil}, refuse approving a pull request with a failing CI
state.

@item code-review-download-dir
The directory binary files are downloaded to; default
@file{/tmp/code-review/}.

@item code-review-db-database-file
The database of reviews and local comments.

@item code-review-log-file
The file errors are logged to; @pxref{Troubleshooting}.

@item code-review-log-raw-request-responses
If non-@code{nil}, also log the raw responses of the forge.

@item code-review-headers-hook
@itemx code-review-sections-hook
@itemx code-review-sections-commit-hook
The functions that insert the header lines and the sections of the
review buffer and of the commit buffer.  Remove a function to hide its
section.

@item code-review-comment-buffer-msg
@itemx code-review-comment-feedback-msg
@itemx code-review-comment-single-comment-msg
@itemx code-review-comment-suggestion-msg
The help texts at the top of the comment buffer.
@end vtable

The forge hosts are described in @ref{Gitlab Instances} and @ref{Github
Enterprise}.

@cindex emoji
To show emoji such as @samp{:thumbsup:} as symbols, enable
@code{emojify-mode}:

@lisp
(add-hook 'code-review-mode-hook #'emojify-mode)
@end lisp

@node Key Binding Suggestions
@section Key Binding Suggestions

Bind @code{code-review-forge-pr-at-point} in Forge's buffers:

@lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'forge
  (define-key forge-topic-mode-map (kbd "C-c r")
    #'code-review-forge-pr-at-point)
  (define-key forge-pullreq-section-map (kbd "C-c r")
    #'code-review-forge-pr-at-point))
@end lisp

Delete local comments and the feedback with @kbd{k}:

@lisp
(define-key code-review-feedback-section-map (kbd "k")
  #'code-review-section-delete-comment)
(define-key code-review-local-comment-section-map (kbd "k")
  #'code-review-section-delete-comment)
(define-key code-review-reply-comment-section-map (kbd "k")
  #'code-review-section-delete-comment)
@end lisp

Move between comments with @kbd{C-c C-n} and @kbd{C-c C-p}:

@lisp
(define-key code-review-mode-map (kbd "C-c C-n")
  #'code-review-comment-jump-next)
(define-key code-review-mode-map (kbd "C-c C-p")
  #'code-review-comment-jump-previous)
@end lisp

The submit commands, such as @code{code-review-submit-approve}, can also
be bound directly, but the Transient menu shows what is available.

@node Doom Emacs
@section Doom Emacs

With Doom's @code{workspaces} module, the review buffer is not added to
the current workspace.  Add it with:

@lisp
(add-hook 'code-review-mode-hook
          (lambda () (persp-add-buffer (current-buffer))))
@end lisp

@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting

@cindex errors
@cindex log file
@vindex code-review-log-file
@vindex code-review-log-raw-request-responses
When opening a review fails, you see @samp{Got an error from your VC
provider} and the error is appended to @code{code-review-log-file}, by
default @file{code-review-error.log} in @code{user-emacs-directory}.
Set @code{code-review-log-raw-request-responses} to @code{t} to also log
the raw responses of the forge, which shows what it sent.

@table @asis
@item @samp{Cannot determine username}
Your username on that instance is not in Git; @pxref{Gitlab Instances},
or @ref{Github Enterprise}.

@item @samp{Required Gitlab token} or @samp{Required Github token}
No token was found in your auth source; @pxref{Gitlab Authentication},
or @ref{Github Authentication}.

@item @samp{Your PR might have diffs too large}
Magit could not parse the diff of the pull request.
@end table

@node Extending Code Review
@chapter Extending Code Review

@cindex forges, adding
Each forge is a class with methods for the generic functions in
@file{code-review-interfaces.el}: fetching the diff, the infos and the
comments, and sending reviews, comments, labels and so on.  See
@file{code-review-gitlab.el} for an example.

